        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 23, \"total_count\": 23, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created listing 'QA Upcycled Side Table' with photo, description, price $42.50, category Furniture, condition Good, location Seattle WA, upcycled toggle on. Detail page displays all submitted data correctly including Upcycled badge, category/condition tags, price, location, description, and listed date.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No edit functionality for existing listings\", \"actual\": \"On My Listings, each owned listing card only exposes 'View', 'Mark Sold', and 'Delete' actions (no Edit/Manage button that opens an editable form). The listing detail page for an owned item only shows a 'Manage Your Listings' button, which returns to the same View/Mark Sold/Delete list. There is no way found to modify title, description, photos, price, category, condition, or location of an existing listing.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Marked 'Mid-Century Modern Armchair' Sold (toast 'Item marked as sold', status badge changed to Sold, button became 'Mark Available'); toggled back to Available (toast 'Item marked as available'). Deleted 'Handmade Macrame Wall Hanging' after a confirmation dialog ('Delete listing? This action cannot be undone') - confirming showed 'Listing deleted' toast and the item was immediately removed from My Listings.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Emma: marked prod-1 'Mid-Century Modern Armchair' Sold and deleted 'Handmade Macrame Wall Hanging'; Browse count dropped from 10 to 8 items, neither appeared in grid. Switched to a different logged-in user (Marcus Chen, non-owner) via in-app logout/login: Browse still shows '8 items available', prod-1 absent from grid, and searching 'Armchair' returns '0 items available'/'No items found' - the sold item is fully unreachable via browse or search by another user, so it cannot be added to cart or requested.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registered Tim QA / timqa.tester@example.com / Seattle WA; got 'Account created successfully!' toast and was immediately signed in (header showed 'Tim QA' user menu, Sell button appeared).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With Condition=Good filter active (category filters cleared), 3 items shown, all condition Good: Yoga Mat $55, Vintage Denim Jacket $65, Harry Potter Book Set $95. Under sort 'Price: Low to High' items were ordered ascending (55,65,95); switching sort to 'Price: High to Low' immediately reordered to descending (95,65,55). Earlier combined-filter tests (Furniture+Upcycled → 2/2 correct; Clothing+Good → 1/1 correct intersection) confirm filters correctly AND-narrow results, and results always satisfy all active filter criteria simultaneously with correct sort ordering.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Searching lowercase 'vintage' matched 2 titles containing 'Vintage' (case-insensitive title match): 'Vintage Denim Jacket - Size M' and 'Vintage Brass Floor Lamp'. Searching uppercase 'PORTLAND' matched 3 items whose location is 'Portland, OR' (case-insensitive location match), including items whose titles/descriptions don't contain the word. Clearing the search box restored the full 8-item result set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Marcus, clicked Add to Cart on prod-9 'Kids Wooden Train Set' (owned by Sofia, not Marcus). Toast 'Added to cart!' shown, header cart icon updated to '1'. Cart page (/cart) shows 1 item with correct title, photo, location 'Austin, TX', price $35, and Total $35.00.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Marcus (non-owner), on prod-9 'Kids Wooden Train Set' (owned by Sofia, available) clicked 'Message Seller', dialog 'Send a message to Sofia Martinez' opened with a textbox and disabled Send Message button. Typed a non-empty message; Send Message button became enabled; clicking it showed visible confirmation toast 'Message sent to seller!' and closed the dialog.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category selection from /categories page does not filter browse results\", \"actual\": \"On /categories, 'Furniture' button showed '2 items'. Clicking it navigated to /?category=furniture, but the Browse page displayed '8 items available' (the full unfiltered set) including clearly non-furniture items (Yoga Mat & Blocks Set, Vintage Denim Jacket, Sony Headphones, Kids Wooden Train Set, Complete Harry Potter Book Set). The Furniture checkbox in the sidebar filter panel was also left unchecked. The category query param is not being applied to filter results.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No seller-facing view of purchase requests or buyer messages\", \"actual\": \"As buyer Marcus, sent a purchase request via cart checkout (toast 'Purchase requests sent to sellers!') and a direct message via 'Message Seller' dialog (toast 'Message sent to seller!') for prod-9 owned by Sofia. Logged in as Sofia (the seller) and checked My Listings, the product detail page (owner view shows only 'Manage Your Listings'), and the header menu/icons - there is no requests inbox, message list, or any indicator/count showing the purchase request or buyer's message anywhere in the seller's UI. The confirmation toasts on the buyer side are the only evidence a request/message was sent; the seller has no way to view the requested item alongside the buyer's message.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Login attempt with unregistered email 'nonexistent-user-9999@example.com' showed 'Invalid credentials' toast, stayed on /login, no session cookie created, header still shows Log in/Sign up when revisited.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Duplicate email (case-only variation) not rejected\", \"actual\": \"Registering a second account with 'TimQA.Tester@example.com' (case variant of already-registered timqa.tester@example.com) succeeded with 'Account created successfully!' toast and created a distinct signed-in account 'Tim Duplicate', instead of being rejected as a duplicate.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Incorrect password accepted\", \"actual\": \"Logging in as emma@example.com with an incorrect password ('definitelyWrongPassword999') succeeded, showing 'Welcome back!' toast and signing in as Emma Green, instead of being rejected.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Marcus Chen: viewing prod-2 (owned by Marcus) shows only 'Manage Your Listings' button (owner view, no Add to Cart/Message Seller). Viewing prod-9 'Kids Wooden Train Set' (owned by Sofia Martinez, not Marcus) shows 'Add to Cart' and 'Message Seller' buttons only - no Mark Sold/Delete/Manage options appear for a listing not owned by the signed-in user.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting with only title filled focused the required Title field (native 'Please fill out this field' validation). Submitting with title/description/price filled but no photo/category/condition showed toast 'Please fill in all required fields' and did not create a listing.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Price field is a number input with min=0; entering -5 triggered native validation 'Value must be greater than or equal to 0' and blocked submission (no listing created, stayed on /create-listing). Attempting to type non-numeric text 'abc' into the price field was rejected by the browser (input type=number), preventing non-numeric price entry entirely.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Inconsistent/incomplete blocking of unauthenticated actions\", \"actual\": \"While logged out, unauthenticated action blocking is inconsistent across the app: (1) Header cart icon click: does nothing (no toast, no redirect, no dialog). (2) Quick 'add to cart' icon on a browse card: does nothing (no toast/redirect). (3) Product detail page 'Add to Cart' button: correctly redirects to /login. (4) Product detail page 'Message Seller' button: opens the message dialog but shows a disabled 'Log in to message' button instead of redirecting to /login (different UX than Add to Cart, though it does block sending). (5) Direct navigation to /cart while logged out: renders a completely blank page (only notification regions, no header/nav/content, no redirect to /login and no message). (6) Direct navigation to /create-listing while logged out: also renders a completely blank page with no redirect or message. While no unauthenticated purchase/listing action ultimately succeeds, the blocking mechanism is inconsistent (silent no-ops, redirects, disabled buttons, and blank unrecoverable pages all occur for different entry points to the same restriction), which is poor and inconsistent UX/constraint enforcement.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No duplicate-account feedback shown\", \"actual\": \"Submitting registration with an already-used email (case variant) produced a success toast and navigated away from the registration form instead of showing duplicate-account error feedback.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing into the search box updated the 'N items available' count and the results grid immediately on each keystroke/fill (e.g. 8→2 for 'vintage', 2→3 for 'PORTLAND') with no separate search/submit button; clearing the box immediately restored all 8 items.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Toggling category/condition checkboxes and changing the sort dropdown each immediately updated the 'N items available' count and results grid with no extra submit action required (e.g. unchecking Clothing while Good was checked: count/grid changed from 1 to 3 items instantly; changing sort from Low-to-High to High-to-Low instantly reversed item order from 55/65/95 to 95/65/55). 'Clear all filters' button instantly restored the full unfiltered set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking 'Add to Cart' immediately showed a toast 'Added to cart!' and updated the header cart icon badge from empty to '1' without any reload; navigating to /cart via the icon (in-app) immediately reflected the correct line item and $35.00 total with no manual refresh needed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Checked multiple listing detail pages (prod-9, prod-10, prod-7). Each consistently displays: photo, title (h1), description, price, category tag, condition tag, location with distance, seller name/location, listing date ('Listed YYYY-MM-DD'). Upcycled items (prod-10) show an 'Upcycled' badge overlay; non-upcycled items (prod-9) omit it, correctly reflecting status. Availability is conveyed consistently: active listings show functional Add to Cart/Message Seller buttons, while a Sold listing (temporarily set on prod-7 for verification, then reverted) explicitly shows 'This item is no longer available' text in place of purchase actions.\"}]}"
